      ":question/math-academy-id": "e-375",
      ":question/problem": "Find the integral of $\\dfrac 1 {2x} + 3x$ with respect to $x.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Applying the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (\\frac{1}{2x}+3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{2x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int 3x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x+3\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}ln⁡|x|+3\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{1+1}}{1+1}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{ln⁡|x|}{2}+\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
    ":knowledge-point/id": "3c865ec2-5bed-5892-966b-a586097be923",
