        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-103374",
        ":question/problem": "Calculate $\\int \\frac{3{x}^{2}-6}{2x}\\,dx.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Applying the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3{x}^{2}-6}{2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2x}-\\frac{3}{x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{3}{2}x-\\frac{3}{x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\int x\\,\\text{d}x-3\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{2}-3ln⁡|x|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
