        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-29915",
        ":question/problem": "Find the integral of $\\frac{\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{5}}}-5{x}^{-1}$ with respect to $x.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Simplifying the exponents and applying the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (\\frac{\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{5}}}-5{x}^{-1})\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{5/2-3/2}}\\,\\text{d}x-5\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x-5\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-4\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-4ln⁡|x|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
